  "articleBody": "Tile surfaces handle plenty of daily wear, but grout breakdown often signals issues beneath the surface that quick cosmetic fixes cannot solve. Recognizing the warning signs helps you protect subfloors and wall framing.\n\nWhen Professional Guidance Helps\n- Missing or crumbling grout joints: Gaps allow standing water to seep behind tile backer boards, risking structural mold or wood rot.\n- Loose or spongy tiles: Movement indicates the thinset mortar bond has broken, which requires tile removal rather than simple top-grouting.\n- Persistent mildew behind sealed lines: Dark stains trapped beneath the surface often mean moisture is migrating outward from within the wall.\n- Natural stone or specialty tile: Marble, limestone, and handmade ceramics stain easily from incorrect grout dyes and require specialized sealants.\n- Large floor surfaces or wet showers: High-moisture areas require precise mixing, proper joint packing, and exact curing times to resist wear.\n\nFor a reliable evaluation of cracked shower joints or aging floor grout, contact HH Remodeling LLC at 303-505-0866 to consult with owner Abraham Becerra.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
}